      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"meritocracy\" myth is a deliberate ideological tool used to obscure systemic oppression, falsely suggesting that outcomes are solely based on individual effort. This narrative conveniently ignores the massive, unequal starting lines created by inherited wealth, discriminatory education, and biased hiring practices. To claim success is purely merit-based is to willfully ignore the structural barriers that prevent marginalized groups from ever competing fairly. Therefore, the concept of pure meritocracy is a convenient fiction that serves to protect entrenched economic power.",
      "source": "target",
